message: "If you reference this research, please cite the consolidated manuscript."
type: software
title: "Discrete Emergent Gravity (DEG)"
authors:
  - family-names: Pinna
    given-names: Matteo
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-4078-9015"
abstract: >
  Discrete Emergent Gravity (DEG) is a research programme investigating whether
  spacetime, gravity, and part of the Standard Model's structure can be derived
  from a single Hamiltonian constraint governing Planck-scale spacetime atoms
  with internal degeneracy g=442 from an SU(21)×U(1) gauge structure. Three
  calibrated inputs are disclosed. Key established results include: SM gauge
  group from group theory, w=−1 exactly, black hole unitarity, the Higgs boson
  mass at 0.19σ from two disclosed inputs, and 17 falsifiable predictions.
  Open problems are stated plainly throughout.
keywords:
  - discrete emergent gravity
  - quantum gravity
  - cosmological constant
  - Higgs mass
  - Standard Model
  - emergent spacetime
  - SU(21)
  - pre-geometric phase
  - falsifiable predictions
